      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "smud:cc-pev-credit-2025-06-20",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "smud:cc-pev-credit-2025-06-20-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 2 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Section II.D states the credit's eligibility in one sentence and the model encodes a wider predicate. Verbatim: \"This credit is for residential customers who have a licensed passenger battery electric plug-in or plug-in hybrid electric vehicle.\" The model's two EligibilityRules are residential customer kind and derType = evChargingDER; urpx:DERTypeValue has nine members with no BEV or PHEV distinction and no vehicle-licensing or passenger-class term, so the narrowing is unexpressible at v0.5.1 and is a blocked deferral. It is currently recorded only in [extraction].notes prose, and the deferrals array is empty on a filing flagged complete = true. (2) Section II.D heads the credit \"Plug-In Electric Vehicle Credit (rate categories RT02, RTL1 and RTC1)\". applicableToRatePlan names smud:tod-5-8pm (RT02) and smud:tod-low-use (RTL1). RTC1 is smud:cpp, a urpx:RatePlanModifier on those same two bases, and RatePlanModifierVersionShape constrains applicableToRatePlan with sh:class urpx:RatePlan, so smud:cpp cannot be named there. An RTC1 customer reaches this credit by holding smud:cpp and this modifier on one base, and URPX states nothing about which modifiers may be held together (urpx-org/urpx#78). The corpus's own R-TOD (Low Use) manifest says the credit applies \"to RT02, RTL1, AND RTC1\".",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-09-22T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
